        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(gateway): preserve emoji in cloud worker failure details",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where a failed cloud worker process could expose malformed Unicode in its error message and persisted recovery state when redacted stderr crossed the 400-code-unit diagnostic limit.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe redacted and normalized stderr is now bounded with the existing UTF-16-safe truncation helper. The 400-code-unit limit, redaction order, failure handling, and worker cleanup behavior remain unchanged.\n\n## User Impact\n\nCloud worker failure diagnostics and persisted recovery errors remain valid Unicode, including when stderr contains emoji near the length boundary.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- AI-assisted: yes. The implementation and failure lifecycle were reviewed.\n- Node 24.15.0: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/gateway/worker-environments/worker-turn-launcher.test.ts -t 'keeps redacted process failure details on a valid UTF-16 boundary'` - 3/3 tests passed across three project runs; 63 skipped.\n- The regression test verifies secret redaction, thrown error text, persisted recovery state, and worker cleanup.\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD` - passed.\n- Focused validation used the local fallback because Blacksmith Testbox was unavailable and sanitized AWS Crabbox could not acquire a lease.\n- Initial CI run [29359486586](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29359486586) completed. Selected build, type, contract, QA smoke, and test lanes passed. The three failing source checks reproduce only current-base debt outside this PR: an unused Bonjour export, a stale QA Lab max-lines baseline entry, and two over-limit system-agent files.\n",
